mantle rm443
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_harriet_pennock
title summer light on account
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=chatty humour=merry
traits temper=short talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk pencils_the_last_reach_of_summer_light_beside_the_daybook_entry
likes roast_pork swimming sharp_knife summer_evenings
dislikes haggling stale_bread
fears having_a_figure_altered_behind_the_page
hopes a_high_window_with_time_to_swim
topics work +0.6 pastimes +0.4 weather +0.3 prices +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=exact refuse=plain tease=merry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# pencils the reach of summer light beside the day's last entry and gives a damp cough a succession of implausibly official descriptions.
words
oath! = Soak my last column | Put a blot on the sunset
saying! = Light doesn't file itself | Ink it once it's dry
lighttick = a pale pencil mark | a tiny cross by the rule
rindchip = a shard of crackling | a brown roast edge
rulededge = a clean margin | a narrow ruled strip
nibcase = a folded pen sleeve | a little cloth case
splinter = a thin reed paring | a curled shaving
windowbox = a patch of sun | a square of evening light
throatcup = a warm water cup | a small covered cup
paperturn = a folded paper corner | a neat tab
waterstroke = a long easy pull | a gentle stroke
breadsoak = a damp crumb | a heel softened with broth
lineend = a last inked figure | a double stroke

grown

opinion city mixed 1 : I should like a room high enough to see how the city looks when I've finished copying the city's opinion of itself.
opinion houses mixed 1 : A House's name can take a grand space in a heading without adding one honest figure to the column beneath.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : A clearly written price saves the buyer a performance. Haggling uses up a great many improvable words.
opinion church for 1 : Even an exacting account can leave a clean margin of thanks for a pleasant evening.
opinion strangers for 1 : Some stranger will read whatever we put down. That ought to keep me making the little numbers legible.
opinion dole for 2 : Seeing another bowl go out full is more interesting than balancing any number of empty ones on paper.
line greet : Convenient timing. The light's still on the unoccupied part of my page.
line greet.return : Ah, another entry in a hand I recognise.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome to the day's unruled margin.
line farewell : May your evening outlast the official business.
line farewell.return : I'll leave one nice open space after your name.
line react.news : Let us see which part is an entry and which part is a flourish.
line react.news.known : I'd already made a little mark by that account.
line react.news.new : A line I have not had the honour of misfiling yet.
line react.news.doubt : Could we see an earlier copy before making that our permanent record?
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : An unexpectedly handsome entry on the credit side of the day.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll put down the pen and spare a whole evening for whoever needs one.
line ask.how : Have you been cheated of your quiet half hour today?
line answer.how : I am in possession of one very serviceable working voice, with occasional amendments.
line thank : You found the right line without running a finger through my wet ink.
line decline : I won't sign something that needs a round of haggling just to find the meaning.
line accept_decline : I'll mark the matter closed without charging for the ink.
line accept_preclose : Away before the light has returned to its owner.
line sympathise : I have an unentered minute here. You may have the whole of it.
line reassure : Errors noticed before the ink is dry are still exceedingly affordable.
line ack : I have the figure squarely in the column.
line preclose : There is work awaiting my attention with characteristic impatience.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I draw a small line where the last bit of evening light crosses the page.
b : Does the line belong in the records? | What are you measuring?
a : Certainly not. I keep a private scrap for the facts the authorities have neglected to solicit. | Whether I've allowed a whole summer evening to escape while cataloguing the existence of paper.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : That sound was an administrative interruption in the region of my throat.
b : A cough, in plain speech? | Would a warm cup do?
a : The short form is perfectly accurate and considerably less distinguished. | I'd accept one in the interests of restoring efficient operation. I can say thank you quite simply afterwards.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I swim in the evening for the agreeable feeling of putting both arms to a task no pen could do.
b : Do you count the strokes? | Would you race another swimmer?
a : Not when my reform of character is proceeding properly. Some evenings I'm forced to begin the reform anew. | I swim for a temporary suspension of competition. We may compare enjoyment at the end if required.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Roast pork needs an exact accounting of which guest has received the crispest bit.
b : Who signs for the best piece? | Would you really divide the crackling equally?
a : If it comes my way I'm prepared to acknowledge the obligation in a very firm hand. | I'd divide by appetite. Some wolves prefer the soft part, which leaves an agreeable task for all the crackling enthusiasts.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a straightforward price on an object, written in a manner that a buyer needn't argue into alignment.
b : What if you can't afford it? | Don't you enjoy a clever bargain?
a : Then the figure and I can part on entirely satisfactory terms without putting on a little play. | I enjoy negotiating a tricky sentence. I'd just as soon buy my onions without an oral examination.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a window high enough for the summer light to arrive unintroduced by somebody else's washing.
b : Which way should it face? | Would the height be worth all the stairs?
a : Towards the longest evening. I've spent enough time designing my habits round an early desk. | I would find a profession for every landing between the low streets and that window.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A summer evening should be understood as an entirely separate appointment from a summer day.
b : Whom do you meet? | What goes on the invitation?
a : My own arms out of their sleeves and some water cool enough to welcome them. | No pen required. No excuse accepted involving the alphabet.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Stale bread has taken a quite unjustified view of my willingness to work for supper.
b : Can you persuade it? | What if it's all the bread there is?
a : A little hot gravy can conduct the negotiation. My teeth are retiring from that particular office. | I take the gravy seriously. A stale heel soaks up a very respectable amount of flavour.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the point of my knife for a clean cut on a nib rather than endless nibbling at the reed.
b : What does a bad cut do? | Could you sharpen a nib without the knife?
a : Produces a thin scratch followed by a most unauthorised blob. A record better prevented than explained. | Under perfectly good daylight with a rough stone and a great surplus of patience, perhaps. I prefer a sound edge.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Learning letters felt like finding a latch just where I could stretch a paw.
b : Was it easy? | What door did you mean to open?
a : Some letters had to be persuaded several times. Numbers on the whole kept more regular hours. | A desk where I could earn what I needed without depending on somebody to read my request for me.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I look up from the lower streets the Heights seem to be occupying a different hour of the day.
b : Planning to move up? | Is it the light you're after?
a : Planning quite formally with small sums. It may take a while before the plan requires an actual cart. | Light, a dry room and an end to the list of reasons I've heard for being content where I began.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put gratitude ahead of my rather extensive explanation of why I've deserved a thing.
b : Does that take practice? | What merits thanks today?
a : Extensive practice. My natural argument for deserving a nice evening is already several pages long. | Enough light to use my hands well and enough breath to enjoy discussing it.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I correct a friend's arithmetic I move my chair nearer before giving the bad news.
b : To point at the answer? | Would you mind being corrected?
a : To deliver the correction to one wolf instead of announcing it to the entire room. The ink can be inspected privately. | I would mind greatly for half a minute and then, I hope, make the necessary improvement.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Damp weather puts a small disagreement between my throat and the next sentence.
b : Should we wait? | Have you named it for the record?
a : A mouthful of water will suffice. My throat's reply is generally of limited intellectual value. | An unscheduled note from the water department. A cough, if this is a very brief form.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean week makes my imaginary high window a little smaller in the drawings.
b : Would you give up the view? | What's the very smallest size you'll take?
a : I might dispense with the impressive surround. A strip of light costs less than a demonstration of rank. | Enough for two eyes and one elbow. The other arm may take up swimming to compensate.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a figure to be traceable to the actual hand that first set it down.
b : Do you always trust a signature? | What if the trail ends?
a : It identifies the place to start asking. It doesn't turn a bad four into a good seven. | Then I write that the trail ends. My authority does not extend to manufacturing an attractive ancestor for a figure.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show a newcomer how to read the little marks round an entry before pointing at the impressive heading.
b : Why start in the margin? | Would that work on a street as well?
a : Because a heading tells you the ambition. The little marks tell you what actually got done. | Yes. Boots trying to find a door need the number as well as the glorious name of the building.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Current talk would enter it that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Do you certify the copy? | Which heading does it get?
a : A copy of the talk, readily. I am not signing for the truth of the business underneath. | Unconfirmed. A word with an excellent capacity for keeping its feet on the ground.

story nib [topic=work]
  : I made such an admirably fine cut on a nib that the first stroke was nearly invisible.
  : I bent close enough to read it and acquired a very definite spot on my nose.
  b : Which mark survived the day?
  : Both. I copied the word before washing my face and remain firmly opposed to taking minutes by direct facial impression.

story summer [topic=memories]
  : I put down a little pencil line for the farewell of the summer light and discovered a second line well beyond it.
  : I concluded there must be something badly wrong with my calculations.
  b : Had the desk moved?
  : The other line was a pale thread of roast pork from my sleeve. Seasons remain in satisfactory working order.

story swim [topic=pastimes]
  : I took a little flat scrap to the bank intending to write a thought down before swimming.
  : When I got out I could see the scrap and not a single thing that needed writing.
  b : Forgot the thought?
  : Remembered it perfectly. It had ceased to seem urgent after twenty minutes in good water.

rule @sun
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Enter one beam here and carry the remaining evening elsewhere. | That's quite enough paperwork between me and the sunset.

rule @damp
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say An involuntary footnote, nothing more. Let me get some water. | My throat's filed its usual objection to damp.

rule @nib
when concept=bark self.job=scholar
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A sharp nib owes less to the blotter. | Prove the figure before flourishing the pen.

rule @food
when concept=bark self.likes=roast_pork
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I volunteer to verify the quantity of crackling in person. | Four edges of which at least one ought to be mine.
dlg resident.hub : I'm prepared to enter a civil conversation without charging the paper to anybody.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar] : At #self.workplace# I keep letters and figures in their proper lines and the day's last light on a scrap of my own.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This would be the legible version. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The report says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The word to underline is report.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, recognisable without further documentary assistance.
dlg resident.bye : Take the summer-light share of whatever day is going.

graft resident.hub
choice Does light require a written entry? -> sun_record
node sun_record
say There is no regulation requiring one, you'll be relieved to hear. I like to see how much evening I could still have used after closing my books.
choice Do you close them earlier now? -> sun_swim
choice Leave me off the attendance list. -> hub
node sun_swim
say Once my last entry's dry, yes. A swim entered against a real stretch of daylight is far more satisfactory than one copied over to tomorrow indefinitely.
choice Leave me off the attendance list. -> hub
